WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.700
Now that we've talked a little bit

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.379
about inheritance and other object-oriented concepts,

3
00:00:06.379 --> 00:00:10.900
I want to now move on about controllers and pawn classes,

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.099
as these do slightly different things

5
00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:17.739
but can be somewhat confusing at first.

6
00:00:17.739 --> 00:00:19.100
So the first thing that we're gonna talk about

7
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.780
is a controller class.

8
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.820
Now, the controller class is a digital representation

9
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.899
of whatever physical input device

10
00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:28.179
is currently being used.

11
00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:30.579
So whether the player is using a mouse and a keyboard,

12
00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:35.060
a controller, a plastic guitar, an Arduino board,

13
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.399
whatever they are using to send out input,

14
00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:42.619
that is gonna be taken by our controller classes.

15
00:00:42.619 --> 00:00:45.759
Now, there are two controller classes that you will see.

16
00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:48.840
There is the player controller and the AI controller.

17
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.359
Now, the AI controller is simply

18
00:00:50.359 --> 00:00:52.439
when you are trying to mimic input

19
00:00:52.439 --> 00:00:55.700
that a player would use,

20
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.140
and it is kind of outside the scope of our talk.

21
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.140
So that's about all we're gonna talk about,

22
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.420
the AI controller.

23
00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.840
The player controller, on the other hand,

24
00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.819
is something that we are going to use,

25
00:01:06.819 --> 00:01:10.659
and controllers do something called possession.

26
00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:14.680
And what they possess is something called the pawn.

27
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.439
And when something is possessed,

28
00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:20.359
its inputs pass through the player controller

29
00:01:20.359 --> 00:01:22.439
down into the pawn,

30
00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:24.760
controlling it and displaying movement.

31
00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.319
So we can think of the player

32
00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:30.159
kind of like a spirit that controls an avatar.

33
00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:33.000
The reason that we wanna do this is,

34
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.620
let's say that we have a game

35
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.519
that supports multiple inputs.

36
00:01:37.519 --> 00:01:40.540
We have mouse and keyboard, we have a controller,

37
00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:45.019
and this game also has multiple vehicle types.

38
00:01:45.019 --> 00:01:48.280
There is a human, there's a horse, there's a car,

39
00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.480
there's a helicopter.

40
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.099
However, what we want to have happen

41
00:01:53.099 --> 00:01:54.640
is that whenever a player is playing

42
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.319
on the mouse and keyboard,

43
00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:58.319
whenever they go to press forward,

44
00:01:58.319 --> 00:02:00.599
no matter if they're a horse or a car

45
00:02:00.599 --> 00:02:02.760
or a tractor or a rocket ship,

46
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.599
we always want W to make them go forward,

47
00:02:05.599 --> 00:02:08.000
A to make them go left, D to make them go right,

48
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.139
and S to go backwards.

49
00:02:10.139 --> 00:02:14.080
And by establishing our movements

50
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.919
and things inside of our player controller,

51
00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:21.460
what we do is we allow our players

52
00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:23.620
to use the same movement components

53
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.060
and the same movement inputs,

54
00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.979
no matter what type of pawn

55
00:02:27.979 --> 00:02:31.180
they're having to be possessing.

56
00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.740
Now, you might be wondering,

57
00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.840
well, you keep talking about this thing called pawn.

58
00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.000
What is a pawn?

59
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.969
Well, a pawn is just simply a class

60
00:02:40.969 --> 00:02:45.270
that takes the input passed from the user or the AI

61
00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.569
and takes that movement and processes it

62
00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:49.770
into the actual movement and interaction

63
00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.090
that you're seeing on the screen.

64
00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.889
Now, when you're dealing with pawn,

65
00:02:53.889 --> 00:02:56.250
you're gonna see two kind of subclasses.

66
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.349
There's a pawn and there is a character class.

67
00:02:59.349 --> 00:03:02.610
The difference between the two is that pawn is a simple,

68
00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.090
basically kind of like a ghost

69
00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.530
that will float in the world and collide with objects.

70
00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.669
The character class though,

71
00:03:07.669 --> 00:03:09.849
that gives us a more advanced movement.

72
00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:11.389
It gives us a capsule component

73
00:03:11.389 --> 00:03:13.370
and a skeletal mesh component

74
00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:18.120
that represents the visual representation of that.

75
00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.759
Generally speaking, all character monsters

76
00:03:20.759 --> 00:03:24.000
and vehicles will derive from either pawn

77
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.289
or the character class, depending on what it's used for.

78
00:03:29.289 --> 00:03:32.490
And again, it's best to keep things split up

79
00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.930
in this manner where we have our controller

80
00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.270
controlling our various pawns,

81
00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:40.289
as this will ensure that we don't have to have code

82
00:03:40.289 --> 00:03:41.889
in multiple locations

83
00:03:41.889 --> 00:03:46.479
and that the end user isn't surprised

84
00:03:46.479 --> 00:03:49.280
whenever a new mechanic is introduced

85
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.500
or they utilize a new type of vehicle.
